# Glossary of Terms

Anything marked **@** is _SquirrelJME_ specific, there may be another
definition elsewhere.

 * _3GPP_ -- 3rd-Generation Parternship Project.
   * This is the organization that has defined 2G, 3G, etc.
 * _ADPCM_ -- Adaptive differential pulse-code modulation.
 * _AOT_ -- Ahead-Of-Time Compiler.
 * _BE_ -- Big Endian.
 * _CDC_ -- Connected Device Configuration.
 * _CLDC_ -- Connection Limited Device Configuration.
 * _CORBA_ -- Common Object Request Broker Architecture.
 * _DIO_ -- Device I/O.
 * _ECJ_ -- Eclipse Compiler for Java.
 * _GCF_ -- Generic Connection Framework.
 * _GCJ_ -- GNU Compiler for Java.
 * _GDB_ -- GNU Debugger.
 * _GIJ_ -- GNU Interpreter for Java.
 * _GSM_ -- Global System for Mobile Communications.
 * _ICE_ -- IMS Communication Enablers.
 * _ICE_ -- Internal Compiler Error.
 * _IETF_ -- Internet Engineering Task Force.
   * This group standardizes _RFC_s.
 * _IM_ -- Instant Messaging.
 * _IMA_ -- Interactive Multimedia Association.
 * _IMS_ -- IP Multimedia System.
 * _ISO_ -- International Standards Organization.
 * _J2ME_ -- Java 2 Micro Edition.
   * Now known as _Java ME_.
 * _JAD_ -- Java Application Descriptor.
   * This is DoJa/Star Specific.
 * _JAR_ -- Java Archive.
 * _JDB_ -- Java Debugger.
 * _JDK_ -- Java Development Kit.
 * _JDWP_ -- Java Debug Wire Protocol.
 * _JIT_ -- Just-In-Time Compiler.
 * _JNI_ -- Java Native Interface.
 * _JSR_ -- Java Specification Request.
 * _LE_ -- Little Endian.
 * _MIDI_ -- Musical Instrument Digital Interface.
 * _MIDP_ -- Mobile Information Device Profile.
 * _MIME_ -- Multipurpose Internet Mail Extension.
   * May also refer to MIME encoding, which uses _Base64_ encapsulated
     within the MIME structure.
 * _MLD_ -- iMelody/MFi, a type of music file used by DoJa/Star applications.
   * There are similarities to _SMAF_.
   * Not to be confused with Sony Ericsson's iMelody format.
 * _MLE_ **@** -- Mid-Level API.
   * This is the API layer between Java code and native code, effectively
     the system call layer.
   * Also sometimes called _Middle Level Emulation_.
 * _MMF_ -- _SMAF_: Effectively _M_usic _M_obile _F_format.
 * _MPL_ -- Mozilla Public License.
 * _NAL_ **@** -- Native Abstraction Layer.
 * _NVM_ **@** -- NanoCoat Virtual Machine.
 * _OMA_ -- Open Mobile Alliance.
 * _PCF_ -- Portable Compiled Font.
 * _PCM_ -- Pulse-code modulation.
 * _PNG_ -- Portable Network Graphics.
 * _RGB_ -- Red Green Blue.
 * _RFC_ -- Request for Comment.
   * This generally refers to the standards put out by the _IETF_.
 * _SMAF_ -- Synthetic music Mobile Application Format.
 * _SMS_ -- Short Message Service.
   * Also known as _text messages_.
 * _SQF_ **@** -- SquirrelJME Font.
 * _SUI_ **@** -- ScritchUI.
 * _TAC_ **@** -- Test, Acceptance, and Compatibility.
 * _URL_ -- Uniform Resource Locator.
 * _URI_ -- Uniform Resource Identifier.
 * _XCAP_ -- XML Configuration Access Protocol.
 * _XML_ -- E_x_tensable Markup Language.
 * _XPM_ -- X Pixmap.
